  "title": "Case surface per role matches the README table",
  "requirement": "The owner of a case can repair it and the observer can record an observation: backend gets case_update and case_verify, reviewer gets case_verify but never case_update, and the README table plus the role's prompt section name exactly the verbs its policy row carries (REQ-179, REQ-182).",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "stale",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/test-cases/test/policy-docs.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/test-cases/test/policy-docs.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Read DEFAULT_ROLE_TOOLS and the README \"Role availability\" table",
    "Compare every preset row of the table with the policy map",
    "Ask sectionText(row) for each row and check it names only the granted verbs",
    "Register one agent per preset through apply() and read the tool names it received"
  ],
  "expected": "backend is registered case_update and case_verify, reviewer case_verify only, critic neither, and the table and the generated section agree with the policy map.",
